  <h1>Holding at Dantian <span class="tag tag-advanced">Advanced · Position 5</span></h1>

  <p>Holding at Dantian is the last of the five foundational postures. Both hands form a ball-holding shape in front of the abdomen at the Dantian, gathering energy back to the Dantian to nourish the original chi. The "Dantian" is the body's energy center, located three finger-widths below the navel. This posture gathers and nurtures the energy cultivated in the previous four postures — it is the advanced stage of Zhan Zhuang for health.</p>

  <div class="callout">
    <h4>📖 Book Reference</h4>
    <p>《The Way of Energy》Part Three, Chapters 6-7: Roots and Branches / Going Beyond</p>
  </div>
  <div class="callout">
    <h4>📺 BBC Reference</h4>
    <p>《Stand Still Be Fit》Days 9-10: Holding at Dantian instruction and series finale</p>
  </div>

  ---

  <h2>Practice Guide</h2>
  <ul class="key-points">
    <li>Both hands form a ball-holding shape in front of the <strong>abdomen (Dantian)</strong></li>
    <li>Imagine steadily holding a balloon — not gripping too hard (it would break) nor too loosely (it would slip)</li>
    <li>Fingers neither over-extended nor tightly closed — maintain a natural, centered curve</li>
    <li>Imagine small balloons under the armpits for support, avoiding shrugged shoulders (shrugging causes neck and chest tension)</li>
    <li>Imagine sitting on a balloon chair (sitting-not-sitting), weight centered</li>
    <li>Sink shoulders, drop elbows, no puffing the belly, no sticking out the buttocks</li>
    <li>Head suspended, body centered</li>
  </ul>

